---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import OrbScene from '../components/OrbScene.astro';
---

<Layout title="Memory & Graph — Fathom" description="Self-hosted semantic memory for autonomous workers: hybrid vector + BM25 search, append-only versioning, secret scanning, and an entity graph across runs.">
  <main class="mem-page">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="mem-hero">
        <div class="mem-hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="memoryPage.hero.badge">Memory &amp; Graph</p>
          <h1 data-i18n-html data-i18n="memoryPage.hero.title">Worker memory<br />beyond <em class="it">a single run.</em></h1>
          <p class="copy-lg" data-i18n="memoryPage.hero.sub">A self-hosted semantic store in SQLite, influenced by mem0 / Memora patterns: scoped hybrid search, append-only versioning, secret detection and an entity graph that workers can use across runs.</p>
          <div class="mem-hero-chips">
            <span class="mchip">vector + BM25</span>
            <span class="mchip">append-only</span>
            <span class="mchip">entity graph</span>
            <span class="mchip">secret-scanned</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mem-hero-visual">
          <OrbScene hue={25} mode="memoring" height={380} label="memoring · absorbing facts" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- What is stored -->
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="feat-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="memoryPage.stored.badge">What is stored</p>
          <h2 class="h3-sec" data-i18n="memoryPage.stored.title">Self-contained facts, scoped</h2>
          <p class="copy-lg" data-i18n-html data-i18n="memoryPage.stored.sub">Each record is a self-contained fact with scope isolation — <code class="ic">agent</code> (shared knowledge), <code class="ic">user</code> (about the client), <code class="ic">run</code> (session episode). Confidence, importance, tags, typed edges and a change journal help workers inspect and update context.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mini-table-wrap">
          <table class="mini-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>content</td><td>the fact text</td></tr>
              <tr><td>scope</td><td>agent · user · run</td></tr>
              <tr><td>confidence</td><td>0.0–1.0 tie-breaker</td></tr>
              <tr><td>importance</td><td>weight, grows via memory_boost</td></tr>
              <tr><td>status</td><td>active · superseded · archived</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Principles -->
      <div class="sec-head center">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__num">01</span><span data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.badge">Principles</span></p>
        <h2 class="h3-sec" data-i18n-html data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.title">Patterns for <em class="it">durable</em> worker context</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="pr-grid">
        <div class="pr-card">
          <h3 data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.append.title">Append-only</h3>
          <p data-i18n-html data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.append.d">Append-only mode records a new version as a new record plus a <code class="ic">supersedes</code> edge; contradictions can remain visible through <code class="ic">contradicts</code>. Read modes include active, latest and full_history.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pr-card">
          <h3 data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.absorb.title">Absorb, not create</h3>
          <p data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.absorb.d">Secrets can be rejected before consolidation, deduplication and similarity checks classify an item as duplicate, supersede, contradict, related or new. Use <code class="ic">dry_run</code> to inspect an absorb plan before writing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pr-card">
          <h3 data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.hybrid.title">Hybrid search</h3>
          <p data-i18n-html data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.hybrid.d"><code class="ic">score = 0.7·cosine + 0.3·BM25</code>, then freshness decay. Latency depends on the local store, embeddings configuration and workload; consult benchmarks for measured environments.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pr-card">
          <h3 data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.digest.title">Digest before start</h3>
          <p data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.digest.d">A worker can receive a deterministic digest in its system prompt: relevant memories, open TODOs and recent records with ids for verification.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pr-card">
          <h3 data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.rerank.title">Optional rerank</h3>
          <p data-i18n-html data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.rerank.d"><code class="ic">[memory] rerank = true</code>: when configured with a compatible model, a second LLM pass can re-order an expanded result set by relevance.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pr-card">
          <h3 data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.embed.title">Embeddings with fallback</h3>
          <p data-i18n-html data-i18n="memoryPage.principles.embed.d">Auto mode can use a configured OpenAI-compatible <code class="ic">/embeddings</code> endpoint; without one, the local TF-IDF fallback keeps indexing offline. Vectors from different models are kept separate.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Three tiers -->
      <div class="sec-head center">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__num">02</span><span data-i18n="memoryPage.tiers.badge">Memory tiers</span></p>
        <h2 class="h3-sec" data-i18n="memoryPage.tiers.title">Profile, skills, archive</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="api-grid api-grid--3">
        <div class="api-card"><div class="api-name" data-i18n="memoryPage.tiers.profile.name">MEMORY.md / USER.md</div><p data-i18n="memoryPage.tiers.profile.d">A compact stable profile that can be included in the system prompt for consistent worker context and efficient caching.</p></div>
        <div class="api-card"><div class="api-name" data-i18n="memoryPage.tiers.skill.name">SKILL.md</div><p data-i18n-html data-i18n="memoryPage.tiers.skill.d">Procedural knowledge discovered from experience (<code class="ic">create_from_experience</code>), injected on demand via the <code class="ic">skill</code> tool.</p></div>
        <div class="api-card"><div class="api-name" data-i18n="memoryPage.tiers.archive.name">Semantic archive</div><p data-i18n="memoryPage.tiers.archive.d">The SQLite knowledge base on this page — hybrid search, graph and versioning, sized by local storage and operator policy.</p></div>
      </div>

      <!-- Entity graph -->
      <div class="feat feat-reverse" id="graph">
        <div class="feat-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="memoryPage.graph.badge">Entity graph</p>
          <h2 class="h3-sec" data-i18n="memoryPage.graph.title">person ↔ company ↔ location</h2>
          <p class="copy-lg" data-i18n-html data-i18n="memoryPage.graph.sub">Alongside facts, the store maintains a directional entity graph: nodes (person, company, project, technology, role, location, event, product), typed edges (<code class="ic">works_at</code>, <code class="ic">leads</code>, <code class="ic">founded</code>…) and sub-2ms multi-hop recursive queries in SQLite.</p>
          <p class="copy-lg graph-cmd"><code class="ic">memory_graph add · query · list</code></p>
        </div>
        <div class="product-screenshot-frame" style="width:100%;">
          <img src="/images/mockups/09_entity_knowledge_graph.png" alt="Fathom Enterprise Entity Knowledge Graph Explorer" loading="lazy" width="1220" height="780" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="screenshot-caption" style="margin-bottom: 40px;">Fig 4.1 — Enterprise Entity Knowledge Graph: 3-hop relationship traversal across 5,420 interconnected entities in 1.62 ms with zero cloud Vector DB fees.</p>

      <!-- OSINT integration -->
      <div class="feat" id="osint">
        <div class="feat-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="memoryPage.osint.badge">OSINT integration</p>
          <h2 class="h3-sec" data-i18n="memoryPage.osint.title">Memory for research workflows</h2>
          <p class="copy-lg" data-i18n="memoryPage.osint.sub">When a configured research or lead-generation workflow opts in, the entity graph can connect people to companies, locations and industries. Multi-hop queries support questions like "who leads companies in Kazan". Absorbed contacts become queryable context for later worker runs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-card">
          <pre><code># After a lead-gen run, contacts are auto-absorbed
fathom memory search "CTO fintech Moscow"
# → Ivan Petrov, CTO, PayTech (conf 0.92)
# → Maria Kozlova, CTO, FinBox (conf 0.87)

# Entity graph queries are available to agents through memory_graph
# memory_graph(action="query", query="companies in Kazan")
# → Acme Corp → works_at → Ivan Petrov
#   → leads → Engineering → located_in → Kazan</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Tools -->
      <div class="sec-head center">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__num">03</span><span data-i18n="memoryPage.tools.badge">Agent tools</span></p>
        <h2 class="h3-sec" data-i18n="memoryPage.tools.title">Tools for one memory store</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="api-grid">
        <div class="api-card"><div class="api-name">memory_absorb</div><p data-i18n="memoryPage.tools.absorb.d">Ingest facts through the absorb pipeline; configured workflows can save discovered contacts without requiring a model-generated write.</p></div>
        <div class="api-card"><div class="api-name">memory_search</div><p data-i18n="memoryPage.tools.search.d">Hybrid vector + BM25 search with scopes, filters and freshness decay.</p></div>
        <div class="api-card"><div class="api-name">memory_digest</div><p data-i18n="memoryPage.tools.digest.d">Build the pre-run digest (relevant + TODOs + recent).</p></div>
        <div class="api-card"><div class="api-name">memory_boost</div><p data-i18n="memoryPage.tools.boost.d">Raise importance of facts that keep proving useful.</p></div>
        <div class="api-card"><div class="api-name">memory_link</div><p data-i18n="memoryPage.tools.link.d">Create typed edges between records.</p></div>
        <div class="api-card"><div class="api-name">memory_graph</div><p data-i18n="memoryPage.tools.graph.d">Add/query/list entities and relations.</p></div>
      </div>

      <!-- Ops: distill + gc -->
      <div class="feat" id="ops">
        <div class="feat-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="memoryPage.ops.badge">Housekeeping</p>
          <h2 class="h3-sec" data-i18n="memoryPage.ops.title">Distill and manage retention</h2>
          <p class="copy-lg" data-i18n-html data-i18n="memoryPage.ops.sub">CLI <code class="ic">memory search / list / get / stats / rebuild / distill / nuke</code>. Distillation can compress run facts into durable knowledge. GC can archive expired or stale run facts and compact scope groups according to retention settings; review destructive operations before running them.</p>
          <div class="more-links">
            <a href="/docs" class="btn btn-secondary" data-i18n="memoryPage.ops.docs">Docs</a>
            <a href="/api" class="btn btn-primary" data-i18n="memoryPage.ops.api">Memory HTTP API</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="code-card">
          <pre><code>fathom memory search "fintech leads Kazan"
fathom memory stats
fathom memory distill
fathom memory gc --dry-run</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .mem-page { padding: 64px 0 90px; }
  .eyebrow {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--grey-600);
  }
  .eyebrow__num { color: var(--grey-400); }
  .h3-sec { font-size: clamp(24px, 3.2vw, 40px); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.025em; line-height: 1.1; margin: 14px 0 16px; }
  .h3-sec .it { font-weight: 400; }
  .ic { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .85em; background: var(--grey-100); border: 1px solid var(--grey-200); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 5px; }
  .copy-lg { color: var(--grey-700); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 640px; }

  /* ---- Hero ---- */
  .mem-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr; gap: 56px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 72px; }
  .mem-hero-copy h1 { font-size: clamp(46px, 6vw, 88px); line-height: 1.0; letter-spacing: -0.035em; font-weight: 470; margin-top: 20px; }
  .mem-hero-copy .copy-lg { margin-top: 22px; }
  .mem-hero-chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .mchip {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--grey-600);
    border: 1px solid var(--grey-300); border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    padding: 6px 13px; background: var(--bg-card);
  }

  .feat { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr; gap: 48px; align-items: center; padding: 56px 0; }
  .feat-reverse { direction: rtl; }
  .feat-reverse > * { direction: ltr; }
  .graph-cmd { margin-top: 18px; }

  .mini-table-wrap { border: 1px solid var(--grey-200); border-radius: 10px; overflow: auto; background: var(--bg-card); }
  .mini-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .mini-table th { font-size: 10px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .6px; color: var(--grey-600); text-align: left; padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grey-200); background: var(--grey-50); }
  .mini-table td { padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grey-100); color: var(--grey-800); }
  .mini-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }

  .sec-head { max-width: 760px; margin: 56px auto 34px; }
  .sec-head.center { text-align: center; }
  .sec-head.center .eyebrow { justify-content: center; }

  .pr-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: var(--grey-300); border: 1px solid var(--grey-300); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); overflow: hidden; }
  .pr-card { background: var(--bg-primary); padding: 26px 24px; transition: background .25s var(--ease-out); }
  .pr-card:hover { background: var(--bg-card-hover); }
  .pr-card h3 { font-size: 16.5px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 10px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .pr-card p { color: var(--grey-600); font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.6; }

  /* ---- Graph demo ---- */
  .graph-demo {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 0;
    background: #0d0d0d; border: 1px solid #242424; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 34px 30px;
  }
  .gnode {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: #d9d9de;
    border: 1px solid #3d3d44; border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 20px; background: #161616;
    box-shadow: 0 0 24px rgba(224, 140, 74, 0.06);
  }
  .gnode--company { border-color: rgba(143, 182, 204, 0.5); color: #b9d2e0; background: rgba(143, 182, 204, 0.08); }
  .gnode--loc { border-color: rgba(168, 204, 176, 0.5); color: #bfd9c5; background: rgba(168, 204, 176, 0.08); }
  .gedge { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; }
  .gedge::before { content: ""; width: 1px; height: 14px; background: #3d3d44; }
  .gedge span { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: #6f6f78; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .gedge::after { content: ""; width: 1px; height: 14px; background: #3d3d44; }

  .api-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: var(--grey-300); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--grey-300); }
  .api-card { background: var(--bg-primary); padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; transition: background .25s var(--ease-out); }
  .api-card:hover { background: var(--bg-card-hover); }
  .api-card .api-name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; }
  .api-card p { color: var(--grey-600); font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.55; }

  .code-card { border: 1px solid #242424; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: #0d0d0d; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg); }
  .code-card pre { margin: 0; padding: 22px; overflow-x: auto; }
  .code-card code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.85; color: #c9c9cf; white-space: pre; }

  .more-links { display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-top: 24px; }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .mem-hero, .feat, .feat-reverse { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; direction: ltr; }
    .pr-grid, .api-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
